---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Enterprise Data Protection | VERIQON TECHNOLOGIES"
  description="VERIQON TECHNOLOGIES Privacy Policy. Learn about our strict enterprise data protection standards, zero telemetry in private mode, and dedicated tenant data isolation for VERIQON ONE."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 5rem;">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />

    <header class="section-hero" style="padding-top: 1rem; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; text-align: left;">
      <div class="badge">
        <span class="badge-dot"></span> Compliance &amp; Trust
      </div>
      <h1 class="heading-xl" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 14px; margin-top: 8px;">
        Effective Date: November 2026 &bull; VERIQON TECHNOLOGIES
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="card legal-content" style="max-width: 900px; padding: 2.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; line-height: 1.8;">
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">1. Commitment to Enterprise Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          At <strong>VERIQON TECHNOLOGIES</strong>, we engineer our software verification products around the foundational principle of zero-trust data isolation. We recognize that application codebases, test fixtures, API schemas, and proprietary database architectures represent our enterprise customers' most sensitive intellectual property.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">2. Marketing Site Data Collection</h2>
        <p>
          This website does not deploy invasive third-party tracking pixels, biometric identifiers, or cross-site tracking cookies. When you voluntarily submit inquiries via our demonstration or walkthrough request forms, the contact details provided are utilized solely for scheduling technical architecture reviews and enterprise evaluations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">3. Zero Application Telemetry in Private Deployments</h2>
        <p>
          For enterprise, on-premises, and self-hosted VPC instances of <strong>VERIQON ONE</strong>:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 1.5rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
          <li>No proprietary customer source code, requirements documentation, or test execution artifacts are transmitted to public LLM providers unless explicitly configured by the customer.</li>
          <li>Local model execution options (via internal enterprise gateways or self-hosted reasoning nodes) ensure that 100% of synthesis and execution logic remains on customer-controlled hardware.</li>
          <li>Cryptographic audit trails and database inspection logs remain exclusively within the customer's owned infrastructure.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">4. Data Retention &amp; Customer Rights</h2>
        <p>
          You may request deletion, verification, or review of any submitted contact information at any time by contacting our data protection officer directly at <a href="mailto:privacy@veriqon.com" style="color: var(--royal-blue); text-decoration: underline;">privacy@veriqon.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md">5. Security Governance</h2>
        <p>
          VERIQON TECHNOLOGIES enforces strict access controls, multi-factor authentication, end-to-end encryption for data in transit and at rest, and regular third-party security audits across all managed infrastructure.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
